	"description": [
		"This course explores topics in American history, designed to emphasize active skills of critical reading, textual and contextual analysis, historiographical argument, and historical writing. Recent topics have included \"Franklin's America,\" \"Women and Slavery,\" \"American Family in Historical Perspective,\" and \"Work in America.\" Primarily for history majors; others by permission of instructor. Offered most years. Counts toward American studies major."
